{"id":"minister-christian","name":"Minister, Christian","aliases":["Minister"],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:minister-christian"],"groups":["Called","Ministers Of","Servants","Influential in public affairs","Expostulate with rulers","Incorruptible","Kindness to:","Sent forth in teams of two","Faithful","Instances Of","Hospitality To","Aquila and Priscilla (Prisca)","Ordination Of","Success Attending","Instances Of Persecution","Zealous"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Minister","text":"One who serves, as distinguished from the master. (1.) Heb. meshereth, applied to an attendant on one of superior rank, as to Joshua, the servant of Moses (Ex. 33:11), and to the servant of Elisha (2 Kings 4:43). This name is also given to attendants at court (2 Chr. 22:8), and to the priests and Levites (Jer. 33:21; Ezek. 44:11). (2.) Heb. pelah (Ezra 7:24), a “minister” of religion. Here used of that class of sanctuary servants called “Solomon’s servants” in Ezra 2:55-58 and Neh. 7:57-60. (3.) Greek leitourgos, a subordinate public administrator, and in this sense applied to magistrates (Rom. 13:6). It is applied also to our Lord (Heb. 8:2), and to Paul in relation to Christ (Rom. 15:16). (4.) Greek hyperetes (literally, “under-rower”), a personal attendant on a superior, thus of the person who waited on the officiating priest in the synagogue (Luke 4:20). It is applied also to John …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G5209","lemma":"ὑμᾶς","xlit":"hymâs","gloss":"","kjv":"ye, you, your","count":100,"share":0.05},{"strong":"H5030","lemma":"נָבִיא","xlit":"nâbîyʼ","gloss":"a prophet or inspired man","kjv":"prophecy, that prophesy, prophet","count":87,"share":0.05},{"strong":"G5613","lemma":"ὡς","xlit":"hōs","gloss":"which how","kjv":"about, after, as, as soon","count":80,"share":0.04},{"strong":"G3056","lemma":"λόγος","xlit":"lógos","gloss":"something said","kjv":"account, cause, communication, X concerning","count":73,"share":0.04},{"strong":"G3972","lemma":"Παῦλος","xlit